[validation.wan_x86_64]
description = "WAN gates (flockGate) — x86_64-musl, depot via HTTPS, mesh via VPS relay"
proven_on = ["flockGate (4/5 e2e PASS — fetch BLAKE3-VERIFIED, launch OK, mesh.init OK, health OK)"]
needs_validation = ["flockGate bidirectional handshake — VPS songbird PROCESS must be restarted (depot binary fresh, running process stale)"]
blocker = """CRITICAL: VPS songbird process on golgiBody has NOT been restarted.
The depot FILE was refreshed Jun 10 02:28 UTC (BLAKE3 03775a3f... verified).
But the RUNNING PROCESS is still the pre-federation-fix binary (predates 1df7ef90).

flockGate tested TWICE (11:40 UTC + 17:26 UTC):
- TCP to 157.230.3.183:7700: CONNECTS (32ms RTT)
- mesh.init: ACKNOWLEDGED by VPS
- After 67s+: latency_ms remains null — no bidirectional protocol handshake

The 4-gate LAN collective works because LAN gates connected differently.
WAN requires the federation fix in the running process.

FIX (cellMembrane on golgiBody VPS):
  kill $(pgrep songbird)
  SONGBIRD_FEDERATION_PORT=7700 /opt/ecoPrimals/plasmidBin/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/songbird server --port 7700 --bind 0.0.0.0 --socket /run/user/1000/biomeos/songbird.sock &

flockGate side is READY (songbird running, port 7700 bound, mesh.init will auto-retry).
Once VPS restarts: expect latency_ms ≈ 30-35ms → 5/5 → stadial criterion 4."""
gate_playbook = """flockGate READY — waiting on VPS process restart only.
After VPS restarts songbird:
  1. flockGate mesh.init auto-retries (already running)
  2. Verify latency_ms becomes non-null
  3. Verify discovery.peers shows transitive peer discovery
  4. Full NUCLEUS health sweep → 5/5 WAN e2e"""

